3]Explain indetail about typecasting ?

	1]Typecasting is the process of converting one datatype into another datatype is called as typecasting
	2]In java thier are 2 types of typecasting:-
		i)implicit typecasting
		ii]explicit typecasting
		
Implicit typecasting:-
======================
->Implicit typecasting is the process of converting the smaller datatypes into larger datatypes is called
as implicit type casting


Explicit typecasting:-
======================
->Explicit typecasting is the process of converting the larger datatypes into smaller datatypes is called as
explicit typecasting, and this has to be done forecefully by the programmer
->During explicit type casting thier is a chance of dataloss


->Among all the 8 primitive datatypes boolean datatype is a datatype which does not participate in
typecasting let it be implicit typecasting or explicit typecasting

->Whenever a char datatype is tried to be converted to other datatype,then that particular character
unicode value will be stored.




4]Is java 100% pure object oriented programming language ?
	->No,java is not 100% pure object oriented programming language because java supports primitive data
	types,although java is not 100% pure object oriented then also we can make java project as 100%
	pure object oriented by making use of a concept called as wrapper classes.
	
->Explain indetail about Wrapper classes ?
	1]In java wrapper class is a class that provides object representation for primitive datatypes
	java includes a set of 8 built in primitive datatypes like boolean,char,byte,short,int,long,float
	and double which represents single value,but this wrapper classes allows this primitive datatypes
	to be treated as objects
	
	2]It supports autoboxing and unboxing
	

AutoBoxing:-
============
	->Autoboxing is the process of automatically converting the primitive datatype into its corresponding
	wrapper class object 
	

UnBoxing:-
==========
	->Unboxing is the process of automatically converting back the object of wrapper class into its
	corresponding primitive datatype.
	
